  "response": "**Working it out**\n\n- Departure: 23:40 on 3 March 2027, Kuala Lumpur time (UTC+8)\n- Convert to UTC: 23:40 − 8:00 = 15:40 UTC on 3 March 2027\n- Add flight time (13h25m): 15:40 + 13:25 = 29:05 → rolls over to 05:05 UTC on 4 March 2027\n- London is UTC+0 on that date (as stated, BST hasn't started yet), so local arrival time = UTC time\n\n**Result:** Arrival is at 05:05 local time on 4 March 2027 in London.\n\nThe \"trick\" here isn't actually a trick that changes the answer — the date rollover (crossing midnight UTC) is the main thing to watch, and the problem pre-empts the BST gotcha by telling you the UK is still on UTC+0. So the answer holds up: 4 March 2027, 05:05.\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 2027-03-04 05:05",
